Article 9 In applying for the establishment of a scenic and historic area, relevant materials containing the following contents shall be submitted:
(1) the basic status of the scenic and historic resources;
(2) the scope of the proposed scenic and historic area and the scope of its core scenic spots;
(3) the nature and protection objectives of the proposed scenic and historic area;
(4) the touring conditions of the proposed scenic and historic area; and
(5) the contents and results of consultations with the owners and right holders of the land, forests and other natural resources as well as houses and other property within the proposed scenic and historic area.

Article 13 The preparation of a master plan for a scenic and historic area shall reflect the requirements of harmonious coexistence between man and nature, coordinated regional development and comprehensive economic and social progress, adhere to the principles of giving priority to protection and subordinating development to protection, and highlight the natural characteristics, cultural connotations and local features of the scenic and historic resources.
A master plan for a scenic and historic area shall include the following contents:
(1) evaluation of scenic resources;
(2) measures for the protection of ecological resources, layout of major construction projects, and intensity of development and utilization;
(3) functional structure and spatial layout of the scenic and historic area;
(4) scope for prohibited development and restricted development;
(5) visitor capacity of the scenic and historic area; and
(6) relevant special plans.

Article 26 The following activities are prohibited within a scenic and historic area:
(1) activities such as quarrying, mining, reclaiming land, opening hillsides, building graves and erecting monuments that damage landscapes, vegetation and landforms;
(2) constructing facilities for storing explosive, inflammable, radioactive, toxic or corrosive articles;
(3) inscribing or defacing on scenic features or facilities; and
(4) littering.

Article 29 The following activities within a scenic and historic area shall be subject to examination by the administrative body for the scenic and historic area, and then be submitted to the relevant competent department for approval in accordance with the provisions of relevant laws and regulations:
(1) setting up or posting commercial advertisements;
(2) holding large-scale recreational activities and the like;
(3) activities that alter the natural state of water resources or water environment; and
(4) other activities that affect the ecology and landscape.

Article 45 Where, in violation of these Regulations, any of the following activities is carried out within a scenic and historic area without examination by the administrative body for the scenic and historic area, the administrative body for the scenic and historic area shall order the cessation of the illegal act, restoration to the original condition or the taking of other remedial measures within a time limit, confiscate the illegal gains, and concurrently impose a fine of not less than 50,000 yuan but not more than 100,000 yuan; if the circumstances are serious, a concurrent fine of not less than 100,000 yuan but not more than 200,000 yuan shall be imposed:
(1) setting up or posting commercial advertisements;
(2) holding large-scale recreational activities and the like;
(3) activities that alter the natural state of water resources or water environment; or
(4) other activities that affect the ecology and landscape.

Article 47 Where, in violation of these Regulations, the administrative department of construction under the State Council, a local people's government at or above the county level, or its relevant competent department commits any of the following acts, the persons directly in charge and other persons directly responsible shall be given a sanction according to law; if a crime is constituted, criminal liability shall be investigated according to law:
(1) establishing various development zones within a scenic and historic area in violation of the plan for the scenic and historic area;
(2) failing to complete the master plan for a scenic and historic area within two years from the date of its establishment;
(3) selecting a unit without the corresponding qualification grade to prepare a plan for a scenic and historic area;
(4) approving construction activities within a scenic and historic area before the plan for the scenic and historic area is approved;
(5) modifying a plan for a scenic and historic area without authorization; or
(6) other acts of failing to perform the duty of supervision and administration according to law.

Article 48 Where, in violation of these Regulations, the administrative body for a scenic and historic area commits any of the following acts, the local people's government at or above the county level that established the administrative body for the scenic and historic area shall order correction; if the circumstances are serious, the persons directly in charge and other persons directly responsible shall be given a demotion or dismissal; if a crime is constituted, criminal liability shall be investigated according to law:
(1) admitting visitors beyond the permitted capacity or conducting touring activities in areas without safety guarantees;
(2) failing to set up signs for the scenic and historic area, road signs, safety warning signs or other signage;
(3) engaging in for-profit business activities;
(4) entrusting the administrative functions such as planning, management and supervision to any enterprise or individual;
(5) permitting the staff of the administrative body for the scenic and historic area to hold concurrent positions in enterprises within the scenic and historic area;
(6) examining and approving construction activities that do not conform to the plan for the scenic and historic area; or
(7) failing to investigate and deal with illegal acts discovered.
